author: claude-code-agent
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "All current pm items and official packages are evaluated from live state; every finding is mapped to a canonical owner or a duplicate-checked focused item; measured regressions include reproducible evidence and fixed non-weakenable budgets; plan captures sequencing across CLI, SDK, architecture, performance, security, multi-agent safety, and packages; no implementation source, tests, dependencies, workflows, thresholds, or release assets are changed; tracker integrity passes; package-owned generated changelog reflects the closed plan; tracker commit is pushed directly to main."
goal: project management = context management
objective: "A deduplicated, evidence-backed roadmap makes pm simpler, faster, safer, more extensible, and easier for agents without feature loss."
value: Future agents can resume from live canonical owners instead of repeating broad review work or creating overlapping backlog.
why_now: "The command surface, SDK, tracker corpus, and official package fleet have all changed materially; current performance and ecosystem-quality evidence must be reconciled before further implementation."
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Whole-system planning review completed and published as a tracker-only roadmap; future implementation remains in the linked open canonical items.
expected_result: "A live-state, deduplicated CLI, SDK, architecture, security, performance, multi-agent, and external-package roadmap with no implementation changes."
actual_result: "Completed plan pm-xe0c38 links all canonical workstreams, records full evidence and sequencing, adds only pm-hcrmye and pm-feecbs, and published the substantive tracker commit directly to main."
